Implemented deferred test comments via `I.comment()` and `I.remark()`.

### Behavior

```js
I.login();
let copyright = yield I.grabTextFrom('div.copyright');
I.comment(`copyright message on page is ${copyright}`);
assert(copyright.indexOf('2016') >= 0);
```

The comment is now added to CodeceptJS’s recorder queue, so it executes at the correct point in the test sequence rather than immediately during test definition. Both method names are supported as aliases:

```js
I.comment('message');
I.remark('message');
```

The methods are non-enumerable, preserving existing actor action listings and compatibility.

