Implemented a source fix for nested sidebar layouts in `lua/bufferline/offset.lua`.

### What changed

Offset detection now recursively inspects nested `row` and `col` layouts instead of only checking the top-level first and last windows. This allows offsets to match sidebars such as `undotree` when the plugin creates a nested window layout.

Your existing configuration should now work:

```lua
require("bufferline").setup({
  options = {
    offsets = {
      { filetype = "NvimTree", text = "Explorer" },
      { filetype = "undotree", text = "Undo" },
    },
  },
})
```

