Implemented a source-level fix for nested sidebar layouts in `lua/bufferline/offset.lua`.

### What changed

Offset detection now recursively inspects nested window-layout nodes instead of checking only direct leaf windows. This allows bufferline offsets to match sidebars such as `undotree` even when the plugin creates a nested split structure.

Your configuration can remain unchanged:

```lua
require("bufferline").setup({
  options = {
    offsets = {
      { filetype = "NvimTree", text = "Explorer" },
      { filetype = "undotree", text = "Undo" },
    },
  },
})
```

